                <pb facs="0743" n="737" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg737"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1481: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-18T11:00:00+00:00">March 18, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—7:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>355. The Palestine Conference ended yesterday when both the Jewish and Palestine
                    Arab delegations rejected the British proposals of March 15 as a basis for
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>The British Government’s announcement of the policy which it will pursue in
                    Palestine is to be made within a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
